{
  "commit_id": "4b8a98ac979df1c7874581d766b82863091a25e0",
  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe OPF gate is now actually in front of the only production flush of queued checkpoint refs: `PushQueuedCheckpointRefs` calls `opfGateForCheckpointRefs` after the policy check and before `flushCheckpointRefsQueue`, so the migration “push now” path can no longer ship 8-layer content without resolving a decision. Fail-closed vs fail-open matches the stated policy (git-refs pre-push warns and continues; the explicit push errors and leaves refs queued), `redact.OPFEnabled()` lives inside the gate, and `doctor migrate-checkpoints` now configures redaction in its own PreRunE so that flag is not a silent no-op. Tests pin rewrite-before-push (trailer, scrubbed sentinel, remote hash) and runtime-failure withhold. Remaining issues are comment quality, not a remaining bypass of the gate.\n\n## Issue counts by severity\n\n- bugs: 0\n- suggestions: 2\n- nits: 0",
  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go",
      "line": 255,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**[suggestion]** The `opfGateForCheckpointRefs` godoc is an 18-line design essay: skip-vs-missing-gate, which caller reports how, why `EnsureRedactionConfigured` is not called here, and that `doctor migrate-checkpoints` needed its own PreRunE because cobra does not inherit a parent's. That last story already lives on the PreRunE it describes. It also cites `setupHookContext`, which does not exist — the hook entry that swallows scanner-config errors is `withHookSession` in `hooks_git_cmd.go`.\n\n**Suggestion:** Keep a short contract (nil proceeds, error withholds, OPF-off is nil; callers must have configured redaction). Point at `withHookSession` if the scanner-config reason stays. Leave the cobra/doctor history on `doctor_migrate.go`."
    },
    {
      "path": "cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go",
      "line": 26,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**[suggestion]** `ErrOPFAbortedByUser`'s godoc still says “PrePush returns it verbatim; the hook command propagates the non-zero exit code so git push aborts.” That is only the git-branch path. This PR also returns the same sentinel from `opfGateForCheckpointRefs`, which `prePushCheckpointRefs` swallows (user push proceeds, refs stay queued) and which `doctor migrate-checkpoints` treats as a clean decline. The new export paragraph covers the doctor case but leaves the first two lines describing a contract the git-refs path does not keep.\n\n**Suggestion:** Split the two backends: v1 PrePush returns this error and aborts the user's push; git-refs withholds the checkpoint flush and does not abort git; doctor migrate matches it as a decline."
    }
  ]
}

